                <section style="-uslm-dtd:section" identifier="/us/sComp/102/228/tII/ptC/s222" styleType="OLC">
                    <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="222">SEC. 222. </num><editorialNote style="-uslm-dtd:legis-comment"><b>[</b>Repealed by section 1351(1) of division A of Public Law 113–291.<b>]</b> </editorialNote>
                </section>
                <section style="-uslm-dtd:section" identifier="/us/sComp/102/228/tII/ptC/s223" styleType="OLC">
                    <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="223">SEC. 223. </num><editorialNote style="-uslm-dtd:usc-reference" role="uscRef"><b>[</b><ref href="/us/usc/t22/s2551">22 U.S.C. 2551 note</ref><b>]</b> </editorialNote><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">DIRE EMERGENCY SUPPLEMENTAL APPROPRIATIONS. </heading>
                    <content style="-uslm-dtd:text" class="block">It is the sense of the Senate that the committee of conference on House Joint Resolution 157 should consider providing the necessary authority in the conference agreement for the President to transfer funds pursuant to this title.</content>
                </section>
            </part>
